.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The routines that return
.B int
return \-1 on an error, and set the error string; a decoder's error says the offset in
the input where it was found.
An encoder's
.I err
is set once one of its writes has failed, and every write after fails.
.SH BUGS
Numbers are not checked when they are encoded, nor is a raw value.
Unlike 9front's
.IR json (2),
there is no tree of values: a program reads into its own structs.
